    "bodyExcerpt": "Skip to content\nFor AI agents: a documentation index is available at llms.txt. Use .md for canonical markdown pages; .mdx is kept as a backwards-compatible alias on supported URL paths.\nassistant-ui\nComponents\nDocs\nProducts\nResources\nPricing\nSearch\n⌘\nK\nAsk AI\n⌘\nI\nCloud\nExamples\nGenerative UI Example\n\nOpen-source React example where the model answers each question in Markdown, with a spec built from the app's components, or with a sandboxed widget, alongside the present tool, Tool UI, and the primitive for backend-emitted `generative-ui` message parts.\n\nsource\n\nfig. 01\nscreenshot\nOverview\n\nThe main route of examples/with-generative-ui answers each question in the format that fits it, using generative-frame with assistant-ui: Markdown for an answer read once, render_spec for structured content built from the app's components, and show_widget for a tool that calculates as the user changes inputs. The model picks the format from the rules useWidgetInstructions adds to the system prompt; Choosing an answer format explains them.\n\nComponents from the kit: toSpecCatalog(styledGenerativeUILibrary) turns the vocabulary, with the registry item's Markdown, Diagram, and Map renderers, into the "
  },
